909263001-f961ec2a-58cc-4a99-9287-370665fc5e1b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"12db90027644a73ed4ab04873c75c7f7fa210f7831e93b7fcc1d6a5f05f08920","event_uuid":"3b05d1bf-5173-4c62-9a91-a53de35645e6","position":{"commit_sha":"5f0b88465cf0db66b16da30e13fe508d85acadd0","position":"1788414883379702001-3b05d1bf-5173-4c62-9a91-a53de35645e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff state. Plan is WRITTEN — it has a `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist, a `## Testing` section, and file_impact already recorded — but it has NOT been plan-reviewed yet, so there is no attestation and it cannot be claimed.\n\nNext step is simply `rebar review-plan <id>`. Do NOT edit the description or file_impact first: file_impact was deliberately recorded BEFORE review, because setting it afterwards invalidates the attestation and sign-review then refuses to re-sign across a changed plan. That mistake cost three re-reviews earlier in this epic.","timestamp":1788398825663860001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review BLOCKED with three findings. I verified all three against the tree; all three are right.\n\nFindings 2 and 3 are the same defect: the plan cited the verdict master as schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json. That path does not exist — ls confirms only src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json. As the reviewer notes, a census reading the cited path would error file-not-found instead of pinning anything. Corrected, and the plan now says the test reads it through rebar.schemas.load(\"verify_signature_result\") rather than by literal path, so the arm cannot break again on a path move.\n\nFinding 1 is the more useful one. AC4/AC5 said \"four registered sites\" and \"four mutation checks\", which matches neither reading of the drift section: five distinct enumerations, or three if counted per document. I had written \"four\" carelessly and it would have left an implementer guessing how many arms to write.\n\nCounting them properly surfaced something the plan had not noticed: the five arms do not share a parse shape, so the census must register ARMS, not files.\n1. reuse-surface.md verdicts — a markdown table with a backticked first column.\n2. oss-comparison types — one backtick span, pipe-joined with no spaces (task|story|bug|epic).\n3. oss-comparison statuses — same pipe-joined shape.\n4. oss-comparison relations — NOT a list at all, but the English word \"six\" in prose. It has to be checked as a COUNT against len(get_args(Relation)) and corrected to \"seven\"; registering it as a list arm would be wrong.\n5. user-guide statuses — one span, pipe-joined WITH spaces (idea | open | ...).\n\nThe plan now carries that arm table explicitly, AC4 requires five mutation checks (one per arm, with the count arm asserting expected-vs-actual count), and AC5 adds the could-not-locate requirement so a reworded passage blames the parser rather than the values — the same failure mode I hit implementing F14.\n\nfile_impact was already recorded and is unchanged, so the re-review runs on the same basis. Re-review started.","timestamp":1788403876140258001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2555 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2555).\n\nWritten RED first: the census was committed before the documents were touched, and all five arms failed naming exactly the drift the plan claimed — verdict table missing key_not_valid_at_era; native-model types missing code_review/identity/session_log; native-model statuses missing idea; user-guide statuses missing archived/deleted; relation count saying 6 where Relation declares 7. Then the documents were corrected and all five went green.\n\nAC4: six mutation checks, each RED with the document and direction named — drop a verdict row (missing [unavailable]), drop a type (missing [session_log]), add a bogus status (stale/extra [frozen]), drop a user-guide status (missing [archived]), change the count word seven->eight (says 8 ... declares 7), and reword the passage so the parser misses it (could not locate).\n\nAC5: adding \"frozen\" to TicketStatus in the master fails the two DOC arms with missing [frozen], proving the expected values are read from the master at assert time and no copy lives in the test.\n\nTwo corrections to the plan worth recording.\n\nFirst, the plan justified the missing verdict by citing docs/identity.md:138,147. That citation is misapplied: identity.md:147 says explicitly that it is describing the verify-authorship gate vocabulary and that it \"is distinct from the separate verify-signature manifest-attestation verdict set\". The drift is real regardless — verify_signature_result.schema.json does declare key_not_valid_at_era in its own enum — so I wrote the new row from the schema's own description rather than borrowing identity.md wording.\n\nSecond, the reuse-surface table opened with \"Common verdicts include:\", a hedge that made it non-exhaustive by construction. A completeness gate over prose that only claims to be partial asserts something the text never promised, so the prose now reads \"The verdicts are exactly:\" and the gate pins a promise the document actually makes. This was anticipated in the plan and is why the fix touches the wording and not only the list.\n\nGates: make lint and make typecheck clean; 425 passed in tests/interfaces/contracts.","timestamp":1788405382866942001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317607113777001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"abb13596-7ba5-41d0-b12e-2cbe77d8ece3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"30a8a237-7ec6-405c-993b-efe6695b1202","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f79d-2a2f-af4e-462d"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F10 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), MEDIUM, ALREADY DRIFTED.\n\n## Verified drift (all three re-checked against the tree, not taken from the inventory)\n\n1. `docs/reuse-surface.md` verdict table lists **8** verdicts; `verify_signature_result.schema.json`\n   declares **9** — `key_not_valid_at_era` is absent. It IS documented at `docs/identity.md:138,147`,\n   so the omission is staleness, not a deliberate exclusion.\n2. `docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md:110-113` \"Native model for reference\" gives types\n   `task|story|bug|epic` (master has 7 — `session_log`, `code_review`, `identity` missing), statuses\n   `open|in_progress|blocked|closed|archived|deleted` (master has 7 — `idea` missing), and the words\n   \"six relations\" where `Relation` declares **seven**.\n3. `docs/user-guide.md:147` says \"Statuses are `idea | open | in_progress | closed | blocked`\" — 5 of\n   7, omitting `archived` and `deleted`, which the SAME file then discusses at `:560,568-571`.\n\nMasters: `src/rebar/types.py:21` (`TicketStatus`), `:23` (`TicketType`), `:24` (`Relation`), and\n`src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json` (verdicts) — read through\n`rebar.schemas.load(\"verify_signature_result\")` rather than by literal path. None of the three\nsites is generated or gated: `gen_api_surface.py` gates library SYMBOL NAMES only and never reads\ndoc prose.\n\n## The arms, counted exactly\n\nFIVE enumerations across THREE documents, and they do not share a parse shape — which is why the\ncensus registers arms, not files:\n\n| # | Document | Enumeration | Shape in the prose | Master |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `reuse-surface.md` | verdicts | markdown table, backticked first column | schema enum |\n| 2 | `oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` | types | one span, `a\\|b\\|c` no spaces | `TicketType` |\n| 3 | `oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` | statuses | one span, `a\\|b\\|c` no spaces | `TicketStatus` |\n| 4 | `oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` | relation COUNT | the English word \"six\" | `len(Relation)` |\n| 5 | `user-guide.md` | statuses | one span, `a \\| b \\| c` with spaces | `TicketStatus` |\n\nArm 4 is the odd one: it is a number word in prose, not a list, so it is checked as a COUNT against\n`len(get_args(Relation))` and corrected to \"seven\". Registering it as a list arm would be wrong.\n\n## One honest complication, handled rather than ignored\n\nThe `reuse-surface.md` table is introduced by \"Common verdicts include:\" — a hedge that makes the\ntable non-exhaustive BY CONSTRUCTION. A completeness gate over prose that only claims to be partial\nwould assert something the text never promised. So the fix corrects the prose to a complete\nenumeration and the gate then pins that promise. The same applies to the `user-guide.md` line, which\nstates a flat \"Statuses are …\". Where a doc genuinely wants a partial list it keeps the hedge and is\nsimply not registered in the census — being in the census is what makes it a promise.\n\n## Approach — add-parity-check\n\nCorrect all three texts, then add `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_docs_enumeration_parity.py`\npinning each corrected enumeration to its code master. The test holds a registry of LOCATIONS —\n(doc path, an anchor that finds the enumeration, the master to compare against) — and never a copy\nof the VALUES, which are always read from `types.py` / the schema at assert time. That is the same\nshape as the existing `test_event_schema_relations.py` docs arm, extended to three more sites; a\nregistry of values would just relocate the mirror this ticket exists to remove.\n\nHouse style is per-topic contract tests (`test_event_schema_relations.py`,\n`test_creation_channel_vocabulary.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py`); there is no\ngeneric docs-enumeration census to extend, so this adds the first one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `docs/reuse-surface.md` lists all 9 verdicts and no longer hedges with \"Common verdicts\n      include\". Verified by the census comparing the table against the schema enum and by reading\n      the rendered table.\n- [x] AC2: `docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` names all 7 types, all 7 statuses, and \"seven\n      relations\". Verified by the census against `TicketType`, `TicketStatus` and `Relation`.\n- [x] AC3: `docs/user-guide.md:147` names all 7 statuses. Verified by the census against\n      `TicketStatus`.\n- [x] AC4: the census FAILS when any one registered arm drifts, and its message names the document,\n      the arm, and the missing or extra values (for arm 4, the expected and actual count). Verified\n      by FIVE mutation checks, one per arm in the table above, each RED with the offending value or\n      count in the message.\n- [x] AC5: the census reads every expected value from the code master at assert time; no relation,\n      status, type or verdict is spelled out in the test. Verified by review of the test source and\n      by adding a value to a master and seeing the DOC arm fail (never a copy inside the test —\n      there is none). A parse that stops matching must report \"could not locate\", not an empty set,\n      so a reworded passage blames the parser rather than the values.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_docs_enumeration_parity.py -q` — AC1-AC5.\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/contracts -q` — no regression in the sibling contract tests.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"add the missing key_not_valid_at_era verdict and drop the non-exhaustive hedge"},{"path":"docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md","reason":"correct the native-model types, statuses and relation count"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"complete the status enumeration at :147"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_docs_enumeration_parity.py","reason":"new census pinning each corrected enumeration to its code master"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","f79d-2a2f-af4e-462d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"f961ec2a-58cc-4a99-9287-370665fc5e1b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a691-f454-92c5-49bd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Three doc enumerations have drifted from their code masters (mirror F10)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["be904eab-6b44-47de-8b56-c57988881b21","200fbe00-89a6-4113-a69e-df64c6e0d9d4","8b39777a-c203-436f-9f47-5d2132434fee","8a122d03-6bff-4471-82c6-a2a1d1f43c52","2941ef24-2a80-4eff-a889-99054d1bfb2c","bead01c9-9a82-4172-aeca-e8460c779534","eed150cf-d504-4b1b-b4da-c8ce906e5610","ea80979d-df35-4386-a5ca-67b58b686155","6e3beca5-fe8d-4414-b74f-b1295024feff","30a8a237-7ec6-405c-993b-efe6695b1202","d298293b-7285-47d5-9a34-e57758ac6c2d","f961ec2a-58cc-4a99-9287-370665fc5e1b","3b05d1bf-5173-4c62-9a91-a53de35645e6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788424625634735001,"uuid":"b6b8d